    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Working: Array Representation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Since A is the root node, we will insert it at the first position (index 1 in this case)."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Inserting the Root Node (A) into the Array Representation",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "B is the left child of A .So, its position in the array is calculated as"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "Position of B = 2 * 1 = 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "C is the right child of A. So,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "Position of C = 2 * 1 + 1 = 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Calculating Positions of Children (B and C) in the Array Representation",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "D and E are the child nodes of B."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Since B is at index 2:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "Position of D = 2 * 2 = 4\nPosition of E = 2 * 2 + 1 = 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Calculating Positions of Child Nodes (D and E) of Node B",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Similarly, F and G are the child nodes of C."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "Position of F = 2 * 3 = 6\nPosition of G = 2 * 3 + 1 = 7"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Calculating Positions of Children (F and G) of Node C",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
